         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Images from Guatemala Kaminaljuyu\n\nThese images are copyright for Guatemala Kaminaljuyu and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 1</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgGuatemalaKaminaljuyu0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgGuatemalaKaminaljuyu0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Maya stela at the Archaeological Site of Kaminaljuyu, Guatemala. Photo taken on <htdate0> (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Playing with Consonants and Vowels - An interactive game to understand how syllables are created. (<htcite1>)</li><li>Multiplying the Findings - an educational game in which the reader visualizes multiplication while exploring different archaeological sites. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part II) - Continuing the challenge, this stage presents sequences that extend up to the billions, deepening the mastery of numerical patterns. (<htcite3>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - In this game, we offer the opportunity to translate numbers from different cultures. (<htcite4>)</li><li>Sequence game (Part I) - In this first stage, learning is reinforced by completing number sequences that go up to the hundreds, helping to consolidate the understanding of basic foundations. (<htcite5>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
